    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1024">

                <pb facs="0923" n="819" xml:id="pg819"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/8255.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-08-06T23:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 6, 1913—11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>397. Today I delivered to the Minister for Foreign Affairs the contents of
                    Department’s August 6, 2 p.m. The President was there and it was translated to
                    him. As far as I could judge it made a favorable impression. The Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs informed me, indeed, that he was pleased therewith.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson O’Shaughnessy</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
